Bind multicast receivers to the wildcard address and join the group on every
socket, as required by BSD sockets.  Construct the listener directly because
network-udp's wildcard path requires IP_PKTINFO, which OpenBSD does not have;
recvfrom is sufficient here because discovery only needs the peer address.
Use SO_REUSEPORT as well as SO_REUSEADDR so concurrent discovery listeners can
bind the same multicast port on OpenBSD.

